state finds: 0
state lynched_syndicate: 0
state lynched_town: 0
state draws: 0
state takings: 0
state faces: 0
state disguised_lynched: 0
state replaced_doctor: 0
state replaced_detective: 0
state debts_paid: 0
state foreclosures: 0
state returned: 0
measure players: players
measure syndicate: syndicate
measure special: syndicate.special
measure asked_for_special: chosen_special != nothing
measure moderator: moderator
measure members: members
measure nights: nights
measure town_left: town_left
measure syndicate_left: syndicate_left + cult_left
measure lynched_syndicate: lynched_syndicate
measure lynched_town: lynched_town
measure draws: draws
measure saves: saves
measure finds: finds
measure doctor_lived: some guest where: it.alive and it.role == doctor
measure detective_lived: some guest where: it.alive and it.role == detective
measure takings: takings
measure faces: faces
measure disguised_lynched: disguised_lynched
measure replaced_doctor: replaced_doctor
measure replaced_detective: replaced_detective
measure debts_paid: debts_paid
measure foreclosures: foreclosures
measure haul: count(haul)
measure haul_needed: haul_needed
measure returned: returned


:: gathering [prologue]
(((
The lobby. Each Linker writes a name; the table chooses how the game is
told; the syndicate is drawn and announced, and only then are the cards
dealt. The draw is random among all ten, unless more than half the table
asks for a special syndicate: then the table votes for one of the four.
)))
{name input for: me.name, max: 24}

{choose input for: moderator, from: moderators, length: 1}

The lamps are lit. Somebody passes round a bottle. Somebody else says *all right, all right, who’s telling it*, and nobody wants to, and so it is decided.

> [[Ask for a special syndicate->gathering]] ~ when not me.wants_special ~ then set me.wants_special: yes ~ id want_special
> [[Draw the syndicate->drawn]] ~ when players >= 5 and not special_wanted ~ for cohort ~ then roll syndicate
> [[Choose the special syndicate->choosing]] ~ when players >= 5 and special_wanted ~ for cohort

:: choosing
(((
More than half the table asked for a special syndicate, so the table
chooses which, by simple majority. A tie is settled by drawing among the
tied. "Surprise us" draws among all four.
)))
--
{ballot for: chosen_special, from: specials, voters: all(guest), ties: draw}

> [[Draw it->drawn]] ~ for cohort ~ when ballot.done ~ then roll syndicate where: it.special == chosen_special or (chosen_special == surprise and it.special != none)

:: drawn
[quote poster]
**{syndicate.name}**
*{syndicate.setting}*
[end]

@lamplighter Among you, tonight, {if members == 1 then "is one" else "are {members}"} of {syndicate.name}. By day they are {syndicate.townsfolk} like the rest of you. By night they are {syndicate.mafia}s, and people are {syndicate.kills}.

[if syndicate.special == doppelganger]
@lamplighter And when one of them kills, they may *become* the one they killed: once each, no more. A face taken leaves no body, only someone missing. Mind whom you think you are talking to.

[if syndicate.special == collectors]
@lamplighter The Collectors don’t kill. They call in debts, two a night. A marked name dies at the next nightfall, unless somebody pays, and the price is a vote.

[if syndicate.special == cult]
@lamplighter The Acolytes don’t kill. They take people into the dark, and only those who voted with them that day. The taken still speak with their old voices. Once there are two of them, they go out on odd nights only, and the One Who Left they can never take again.

[if syndicate.special == heist]
@lamplighter Nobody dies this weekend. Something, every night, goes missing. {haul_needed} keepsakes in the Crew’s bag and they’re off on the morning train.

[end]
> [[Deal the cards->dealt]] ~ for cohort ~ then shuffle roles ~ then deal 1 from roles to each hand ~ then shuffle keepsakes ~ then deal 1 from keepsakes to each keepsake

:: dealt
(((
Each player sees only their own card. `{present linker}` is the Linker
reading this, so each sees their own name and role; the Storyteller sees
everyone's.
)))
set me.role: top of my hand
set me.team: mafia when me.role == mafia and syndicate.special != cult
set me.team: cult when me.role == mafia and syndicate.special == cult
--
[if me.is(storyteller)]
You look round the table at every card. {list hand of each guest ~ one per line}

[else]
{present linker}, you turn your card over under your hand.

[if me.role == mafia]
You are a **{syndicate.mafia}**.

[if me.role == mafia and members == 1]
You are alone. Nobody at this table is with you.

[if me.role == mafia and members > 1]
The others are {all(guest, where: it.team == me.team and it != me)}.

[if me.role == doctor and syndicate.special != collectors and syndicate.special != cult]
You are **{syndicate.doctor}**. Each night you may save someone; never the same one two nights running.

[if me.role == doctor and syndicate.special == collectors]
You are **{syndicate.doctor}**. Each night you may take someone in, and no Collector marks a name under your roof; never the same one two nights running.

[if me.role == doctor and syndicate.special == cult]
You are **{syndicate.doctor}**. You were in the dark once, and you got out, and you will never go back: the lamp cannot take you again. So you never sit up for yourself. Each night you may sit up with someone else and keep them turned from the light; never the same one two nights running.

[if me.role == detective]
You are **{syndicate.detective}**. Each night you may look into someone, and learn which side they are on.

[if me.role == townsfolk]
You are a **{syndicate.townsfolk}**. You have your wits, your vote, and your neighbours.

[if syndicate.special == heist]
In front of you lies your keepsake: **{top of my keepsake}**.

[end]
> [[Night falls->night]] ~ for cohort ~ then wait until night

:: night
(((
Debts fall due at nightfall: a name marked this morning, and not paid
today, dies now.
)))
let due: all(guest, where: it.alive and it.marked and it.marked_since < clock.now)
set due.alive: no when syndicate.special == collectors
raise foreclosures count(due) when syndicate.special == collectors
set foreclosed: due when syndicate.special == collectors
raise nights 1
(((
Night: each acts in private. Every target is `~ at guest` with a `where:`
that says which guests may be picked. Links grouped by who may take them.
The syndicate chooses together: `~ consensus` makes the Link a vote among
those who may take it, and the most-chosen target is the one. A consensus
remembers who chose each target, in the order they placed that vote
(changing a vote places it again): `victim.chosen_by`, first to last.
Where one member does the deed for all (the Doppelgänger who takes the
face, the thief who carries the keepsake), it is the first who placed
their vote on the target chosen: `first(victim.chosen_by)`. So it pays to
decide quickly.

The Collectors choose two: `~ consensus 2` makes each member choose two
names, and the two most chosen are `targets`, most chosen first. The Cult,
once it has two Acolytes, goes out on odd nights only.
)))
--
[if me.alive]
Night in {syndicate.setting}. Eyes closed, if you please.

[else]
{syndicate.dead}

[end]
[if me.alive and me.team == cult and cult_left >= 2 and nights mod 2 == 0]
The lamp is dark tonight. The Long Night keeps its own calendar: tomorrow it turns again.

[end]
> ~ for guest where: it.alive and it.team == mafia and syndicate.special == none ~ consensus
> [[{capital(syndicate.kills)}: {target}->night:done]] ~ at guest where: it.alive and it.team != mafia ~ then set victim: target

(((
The Doppelgänger Clan. Each vote carries its voter's way of doing it:
`me.method`. The one who does the deed (the first to vote for the victim
chosen) does it their way. Each member may take a face once: a
replacement the Doctor stops does not use it up.
)))
> ~ for guest where: it.alive and it.team == mafia and syndicate.special == doppelganger ~ consensus
> [[Replace {target}->night:done]] ~ at guest where: it.alive and it.team != mafia ~ when not me.swapped ~ then set victim: target ~ then set me.method: replace
> [[Kill {target} and keep your own face->night:done]] ~ at guest where: it.alive and it.team != mafia ~ then set victim: target ~ then set me.method: kill

> ~ for guest where: it.alive and it.team == mafia and syndicate.special == collectors ~ consensus 2
> [[Mark {target}->night:done]] ~ at guest where: it.alive and not it.marked and it.team != mafia ~ then set victim: first(targets) ~ then set second: last(targets)

> ~ for guest where: it.alive and it.team == cult ~ consensus ~ when cult_left < 2 or nights mod 2 == 1
> [[Take {target} into the dark->night:done]] ~ at guest where: it.alive and it.team != cult and it.role != doctor and it.voted_with(cult) ~ then set victim: target

> ~ for guest where: it.alive and it.team == mafia and syndicate.special == heist ~ consensus
> [[Lift {target}’s {top of target.keepsake}->night:done]] ~ at guest where: it.alive and it.team != mafia and count(it.keepsake) > 0 ~ then set victim: target

> ~ for guest where: it.alive and it.role == doctor
> [[Save {target}->night:done]] ~ at guest where: it.alive and it != me.saved_last ~ when syndicate.special != collectors and syndicate.special != cult ~ then set saved: target ~ then set me.saved_last: target
> [[Take {target} in->night:done]] ~ at guest where: it.alive and it != me.saved_last ~ when syndicate.special == collectors ~ then set saved: target ~ then set me.saved_last: target
> [[Sit up with {target}->night:done]] ~ at guest where: it.alive and it != me and it != me.saved_last ~ when syndicate.special == cult ~ then set saved: target ~ then set me.saved_last: target

> ~ for guest where: it.alive and it.role == detective
> [[Look into {target}->night:looked]] ~ at guest where: it.alive and it != me ~ then assert {{ target guilty }} in findings when target.team != town ~ then assert {{ target innocent }} in findings when target.team == town ~ then raise finds 1 when target.team != town

> [[Sleep->night:done]] ~ for guest where: it.alive and it.role == townsfolk
> [[Wait for morning->night:done]] ~ for guest where: not it.alive or it.is(storyteller)

> [[Dawn->morning]] ~ for cohort ~ after 2m ~ id dawn ~ then wait until day

:: night:looked
(((
The Detective asks one question, the classic one: *is this one of them?*
Yes means one of them: the syndicate, or the Cult's taken. Findings are
kept as `{{ x guilty }}` or `{{ x innocent }}` in the Detective's own
knowledge.
)))
--
Is {target} one of them? You find out, by ways of your own.

[if target.team != town]
**Yes.**

[else]
**No.**

[end]
> [[Back to bed->night:done]] ~ id back_to_bed

:: night:done
(((
Waits for everyone. When the last player has chosen, the night is over.
The night has a deadline too: Dawn, on the night's first page, is taken
by itself two minutes after nightfall, wherever each player has got to.
The votes cast by then count (`~ consensus`, milestone 21d), and a
syndicate that has cast none kills nobody.
)))
--
You wait for the others.

> [[Morning->morning]] ~ for cohort ~ when cohort.all.chose ~ then wait until day

:: morning
(((
The morning report. What the night did is settled here, in order; then
it is told, three ways. Every special's night choice lands here, not on
its Link, so the save can stop any of them: a death, a theft, a mark, a
taking. `report` holds the table's version; MonkeyPaw or
the Storyteller may tell it differently.
)))
let flourish: one(syndicate.deaths)
(((
Who does the deed for the syndicate: the first member who placed their
vote on the target chosen.
)))
let first_voter: first(victim.chosen_by)
let replacing: syndicate.special == doppelganger and first_voter.method == replace
let taken: top of victim.keepsake
set taken.owner: victim when syndicate.special == heist and victim != nobody
set report: "A quiet night. Too quiet, somebody says, and is told to shut up."
let foiled_second: second != nobody and second == saved
let foiled: (victim != nobody and victim == saved) or foiled_second
set victim: nobody when victim == saved
set second: nobody when foiled_second
set second.marked: yes when second != nobody and syndicate.special == collectors
set second.marked_since: clock.now when second != nobody and syndicate.special == collectors
set victim.alive: no when victim != nobody and syndicate.special in [none, doppelganger]
set victim.marked: yes when victim != nobody and syndicate.special == collectors
set victim.marked_since: clock.now when victim != nobody and syndicate.special == collectors
set victim.team: cult when victim != nobody and syndicate.special == cult
teach victim cult_secret when victim != nobody and syndicate.special == cult
teach victim cult_calendar when victim != nobody and syndicate.special == cult
(((
The Doppelgänger's swap happens before the report is written. The killer
(the first who voted for the victim, by their own method) wears the
victim's face from now on; the victim's seat, out of the game, carries the
killer's old name, and the report calls that name missing: there is no
body. One face each.
)))
set first_voter.shown_as: victim.name when replacing and victim != nobody
set victim.shown_as: first_voter.name when replacing and victim != nobody
set first_voter.swapped: yes when replacing and victim != nobody
raise replaced_doctor 1 when replacing and victim != nobody and victim.role == doctor
raise replaced_detective 1 when replacing and victim != nobody and victim.role == detective
move taken to first_voter.loot when syndicate.special == heist and victim != nobody
raise saves 1 when foiled
raise takings 1 when victim != nobody and syndicate.special == cult
raise faces 1 when victim != nobody and replacing
(((
The taking is secret, and a mark is read from the slate, so only deaths
and thefts make the report.
)))
set report: "{victim} {flourish}." when victim != nobody and syndicate.special in [none, doppelganger, heist] and not replacing
set report: "{victim} is missing. There is no body, and nobody died." when victim != nobody and replacing
set report: "Nobody died. Someone at this table will never know how close it came." when foiled and syndicate.special in [none, doppelganger]
set report: "The Collector knocked at a lodging house last night. {capital(syndicate.doctor)} said there was nobody of that name living there." when foiled and syndicate.special == collectors
set report: "Somebody sat up all night with their back to the window, and somebody who used to love the lamp talked to them until dawn." when foiled and syndicate.special == cult
--
[if replacing and victim != nobody; then play morning:replaced]
[if syndicate.special == collectors; then play morning:debts]
[if syndicate.special == heist and victim != nobody; then play morning:missing]

[if me.heard and rumour_about != nobody]
Somebody leaned over at breakfast and told you something about {rumour_about}. You are not sure it is true. You are not sure it isn’t.

(((
What happened, plainly, whoever tells it: a MonkeyPaw or a Storyteller may
tell the night their way, but never instead of the facts.
)))
[if moderator != engine and victim != nobody and syndicate.special in [none, doppelganger] and not replacing]
@lamplighter Gone in the night: {victim}.

[if moderator != engine and victim != nobody and replacing]
@lamplighter Missing in the night: {victim}. Nobody died.

[if moderator == engine]
@lamplighter {report}

[if moderator == monkeypaw]
{embed nib: "morning:told"}

[if moderator == storyteller and me.is(storyteller)]
The table’s version: *{report}*. Tell it your way, or let it stand.

{text input for: report, max: 600}

[if moderator == storyteller and not me.is(storyteller)]
@storyteller {report}

[end]
> [[Talk it over->day]] ~ for cohort ~ id to_day
~ then set victim: nobody ~ then set second: nobody ~ then set saved: nobody

:: morning:told
(((
A pending passage that is not a fork: MonkeyPaw writes this morning's
report to the syndicate's voice, from the facts of the night; if nothing
comes in time, the table's line is read instead.
)))
pending: by monkeypaw ~ brief morning ~ timeout 10s
--
@lamplighter {report}

:: morning:replaced
(((
The Doppelgänger. The clan member who killed wears the victim's face from
now on: the platform shows the killer's seat under the victim's name, and
the morning reports the killer's old name missing. Names are swapped (in
the morning's header); roles are not. A swap is a clue the town is meant
to have: one of the living is not who they seem.
)))
--
At first light, a bed not slept in: {possessive(victim)}. The sanatorium is searched from the boiler room to the bell. There is no one to find.

(((
No pronouns here: they would be the victim's, and give the swap away.
)))

:: morning:debts
--
[if count(foreclosed) > 0]
@lamplighter At nightfall the Collectors called on {all foreclosed}. {capital(plural(count(foreclosed), "account"))} closed.

[end]
@lamplighter On the Collectors’ slate this morning: {all(guest, where: it.alive and it.marked)}.

:: morning:missing
--
@lamplighter In the night, from {victim}’s dressing table: one {taken}. The house is searched. Nothing is found. The house is very large.

:: day
(((
Day: the talk happens at the table (or in the platform's chat); the
engine keeps the clock and the vote. Paying a debt costs your vote.
Whispers: once a game, anyone alive may start a rumour; each morning it
spreads to the next seat that hasn't heard it.
)))
--
[if me.alive]
You have five minutes. Make them count.

[end]
> [[Pay {target}’s debt->day]] ~ at guest where: it.alive and it.marked ~ when syndicate.special == collectors and me.alive and not me.voteless ~ then set target.marked: no ~ then set me.voteless: yes ~ then raise debts_paid 1 ~ id pay_debt
> [[Start a whisper about {target}->day:whisper]] ~ at guest where: it.alive and it != me ~ when me.alive and not whispered ~ id whisper
> [[To the vote->vote]] ~ for cohort ~ after 5m ~ id to_vote

:: day:whisper
set whispered: yes
set rumour_about: target
set me.heard: yes
--
You lean to your neighbour and say, very quietly, something about {target} that you are not sure is true. By tomorrow it will be in the next ear, and the next.

[end]
> [[Back to the table->day]] ~ id back_to_table

:: vote
(((
The vote. Only the living vote, and not those who paid a debt today:
`voters:` is a `where:` too. The dead watch. A tie votes once more, then
is drawn by lot among the tied: someone leaves the table every day, so
every game ends, even one where nobody can be killed at night.
)))
--
{accuse who: all(guest, where: it.alive), voters: all(guest, where: it.alive and not it.voteless), revote: 1, ties: draw}

> [[The vote is counted->counted]] ~ for cohort ~ when accusation.done

:: counted
set lynched: accusation.who
set lynched.alive: no
raise lynched_syndicate 1 when lynched.team != town
raise lynched_town 1 when lynched.team == town
raise disguised_lynched 1 when lynched.shown_as != lynched.name
raise draws 1 when accusation.drawn
set each guest.voteless: no
(((
A thief voted out is searched: what they stole goes back to its owners,
and can be stolen again.
)))
let found: lynched.loot
move each found to it.owner.keepsake when syndicate.special == heist
raise returned count(found) when syndicate.special == heist
spreads 1 to nearest(guest, where: it.alive and not it.heard) ~ along seat ~ then set it.heard: yes ~ when whispered
--
{ballots}

@lamplighter {lynched} it is. {capital(lynched.they)} turn{if lynched.pronouns == they then "" else "s"} over {possessive(lynched)} card:

[if syndicate.special == doppelganger and lynched.shown_as != lynched.name]
@lamplighter …and under the face of {lynched}, something else. {lynched.name}. A {syndicate.mafia}.

[if not (syndicate.special == doppelganger and lynched.shown_as != lynched.name)]
@lamplighter {if lynched.team == town then syndicate.townsfolk else syndicate.mafia}.

[if syndicate.special == heist and count(found) > 0]
@lamplighter In {possessive(lynched)} luggage, wrapped in a shirt: {all found}. Each goes back to its owner, who pretends not to have been worried.

[end]
> [[Night falls->night]] ~ for cohort ~ id night_again ~ then wait until night

:: town_wins [finale]
finale when: no guest where: it.alive and it.team != town
--
@lamplighter The last of {syndicate.name} is gone. In {syndicate.setting}, the town sleeps with its doors unlocked, for one night at least.

> [[The cards->reveal]] ~ for cohort

:: syndicate_wins [finale]
finale when: syndicate_left >= town_left and syndicate.special in [none, doppelganger, collectors]
--
@lamplighter There are as many {syndicate.mafia}s at the table now as anyone else, and so there are no longer anyone else. {capital(syndicate.name)} have won.

> [[The cards->reveal]] ~ for cohort

:: cult_wins [finale]
finale when: syndicate.special == cult and cult_left > town_left
--
@lamplighter The lamp in the lighthouse turns, and turns, and on the island nobody looks at the sea any more. They look at the lamp.

> [[The cards->reveal]] ~ for cohort

:: heist_wins [finale]
finale when: syndicate.special == heist and count(haul) >= haul_needed
--
@lamplighter Monday. The morning train pulls out of the halt with {members} {plural(members, "guest")} fewer than came, and {haul_needed} keepsakes: {all haul}. The Inspector writes it up as a misunderstanding.

> [[The cards->reveal]] ~ for cohort

:: reveal [epilogue]
--
The cards go face up, all at once:

{list hand of each guest ~ one per line}

[if syndicate.special == doppelganger]
And the faces: {all(guest, where: it.shown_as != it.name)} {if count(guest, where: it.shown_as != it.name) == 1 then "was" else "were"} not who they seemed.

[if syndicate.special == heist and count(haul) > 0]
And the luggage: {list loot of each guest where count(it.loot) > 0 ~ one per line}

[end]

:: five_players_one_syndicate [test]
start: gathering ~ cohort 5
given: draw syndicate vampires
do: "Draw the syndicate"
do: "Deal the cards"
expect: syndicate_left == 1
expect: count(guest, where: it.role == doctor) == 1
expect: count(guest, where: it.role == detective) == 1

:: the_doctor_cannot_save_twice [test]
start: night ~ cohort 5 ~ as doctor_player
given: draw syndicate vampires
given: set me.saved_last: guest_2
expect no link: "Save {guest_2}"

:: the_dead_do_not_vote [test]
start: vote ~ cohort 6
given: set guest_3.alive: no
expect: not guest_3.in(accusation.voters)

:: a_name_taken_in_is_not_marked [test]
start: morning ~ cohort 5
given: draw syndicate collectors
given: set victim: guest_2
given: set saved: guest_2
expect: not guest_2.marked

:: a_guest_sat_up_with_is_not_taken [test]
start: morning ~ cohort 5
given: draw syndicate cult
given: set victim: guest_2
given: set saved: guest_2
expect: guest_2.team == town

:: the_town_wins_when_none_are_left [test]
start: counted ~ cohort 5
given: set each guest.team: town
expect at: town_wins
expect events: ending_reached
